Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?SystemUI:=20Bud=C3=ADk=20control=20centre=20fro?=
 =?UTF-8?q?m=20the=20top,=20in=20modules=20like=20iOS?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The control centre was a dark sheet anchored to the bottom edge with a
row of unlabelled keys, large keys and a segmented brightness bar. It is
now laid out from the top of the sheet like the iOS / HyperOS control
centre, in a grid of four square cells:

- connectivity module (2 x 2): the first four of Wi-Fi / internet,
  Bluetooth, mobile data, airplane mode and hotspot as round keys;
- media module (2 x 2): title, artist, previous / play-pause / next, or
  "Nic nehraje";
- brightness and volume as two cell high sliders filled with mint from
  the bottom; a drag moves the value by the distance moved and only
  redraws the slider;
- the other tiles as one cell keys (icon, name when it fits); a long
  press opens the tile's details or settings;
- edit, settings and power keys below; a tap on empty space closes.

Every module is placed by a dense packing in one Layout, measured once.
Colours follow the light / dark mode (the whole sheet, not only the
keys). The sheet is drawn without the offscreen layer and the shaped
clip, and the content scrolls without the stretch overscroll, which
redrew the whole panel on the GPU while it moved.

The editor keeps tiles in sysui_qs_tiles and shows them in the same
grid; Settings.Secure budik_cc_blocks now only switches the media,
brightness and volume modules off ("!NAME"), older values still parse.
The media volume slider view model is always created.
